      "message": "feat(player): add network-aware Wi-Fi vs Cellular audio quality ceilings\n\n- Introduce separate audio quality settings for Wi-Fi and Cellular connections under Player & Audio Settings, following Nothing OS 5.0 design principles.\n- Add AudioQuality enum metadata with bitrate ceilings, descriptive labels, and estimated hourly data usage (Lossless 300+ MB/hr, High 144 MB/hr, Medium 77 MB/hr, Low 29 MB/hr).\n- Implement dynamic network evaluation in MusicService via getEffectiveAudioQuality(), checking ConnectivityManager.isActiveNetworkMetered and DataSaver settings.\n- Gate high-bandwidth addon FLAC/ALAC stream resolution behind Lossless/High ceilings to protect mobile data plans.\n- Update YTPlayerUtils to respect audio quality ceilings when extracting streams.\n- Add localized strings for Wi-Fi and Cellular quality preferences.",
