      },
      "message": "fix(auto): serve artwork as content URIs and keep Home shelves stable\n\nAndroid Auto and the instrument cluster only load content:// or\nandroid.resource:// artwork, but items carried https:// URLs. Embedded\nbytes covered only part of each page, so covers were missing on the\ncluster, in the 1/3 layout and on long lists.\n\n- Add AutomotiveArtworkProvider serving HMAC-signed content:// URIs\n  backed by Coil and a small file cache; map browse/search items and\n  the session's now-playing metadata (SessionArtworkPlayer) to them.\n- Cache decoded covers in CoilBitmapLoader and prefetch the current and\n  next queue items, so the first metadata update for a track already\n  carries its bitmap; drop the replaceMediaItem embedding.\n- Load every Home page, key shelves by title, merge fetches into one\n  snapshot persisted across restarts, and serve it stale-while-\n  revalidate so shelves no longer come and go.\n- Retry missing maxresdefault/sddefault YouTube thumbnails with\n  hqdefault via a Coil interceptor; fix yt3.ggpht resize.",
