      },
      "message": "fix(auto): address review findings, harden addon matching and Auto artwork\n\nCodeRabbit follow-up on #665 plus reported playback/browse issues.\n\n- resolveStream: classify host-wide connection failures only at the\n  call.execute() boundary; response-body read/JSON parse errors no longer\n  stop the searchBases loop from trying viable alternatives.\n- AutomotiveArtwork.attachAll: await each chunk before starting the next so\n  at most MAX_CONCURRENT_LOADS (4) artwork loads run at once.\n- AutomotiveArtwork: add an 8 MB in-memory cover cache so the dashboard/\n  cockpit reuses covers already resolved by any surface instead of\n  re-decoding with a cold Coil cache and shipping no artwork.\n- selectBestMatch: artist agreement is now a gate (no more same-title,\n  different-artist matches); requested version qualifiers (remix, live,\n  instrumental, ...) must be present, so a remix is not replaced by the\n  plain original; credits (feat/ft/prod) stay tolerated.\n- MediaLibrarySessionCallback: serve one cached YouTube Home snapshot\n  (5 min TTL) across all automotive browse calls so shelves such as\n  'Mixtape per te' no longer appear/disappear between visits and section\n  indices stay consistent.",
